  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC Phase out Management plan stage III in Cameroon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The HCFC Phase-Out Management Plan (HPMP) Stage III for Cameroon aims to further reduce the consumption of HCFC in alignment with the Montreal Protocol&apos;s targets. This project focuses on transitioning to low Global Warming Potential (GWP) alternatives in the refrigeration and air conditioning sectors. Key activities include updating regulations, conducting training workshops for service technicians and customs officers, and promoting environmentally friendly technologies. Coordinated by the National Ozone Office with support from UNIDO, the project leverages robust legal frameworks and stakeholder engagement to ensure sustainable implementation and significant climate benefits.</narrative>
  </description>
